                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "EDIT: Since my review, the dev has updated the game, and believes they have fixed a number of issues. I have not confirmed this, but feel it's worth noting.\n\nORIGINAL REVIEW:\n\nGemstone Keeper is a solid foundation in an unfinished game.\n\nThe shooting mechanics, enemy behaviours, weapon combinations and art are well done and feel good, but between bugs, design failures, boring procedural generation, and just a lack of content overall, I don't think this game is ready for general consumption.\n\nIssues I had include:\n\nOnly being able to see keybinds when you start a new game.\n\nRandomly not being able to start from the depth I got to on the last run.\n\nNot knowing what stats do.\n\nThere are 5 bosses, and by the time you've reached the second, you've probably bought all the weapons and seen everything the procedural generation can throw at you, then it's just grinding through a lot of samey levels until you reach the end.\n\nThe last boss relies on shields to stop you shooting it until you can break through for a hit, except one of the weapons is piercing, so it just ignores the shields and kills the boss in seconds.\n\nAfter a while, you can afford to buy a hundred medkits, buff your health, and then just tank from one end of the game to the other.\n\nIf you're curious about other issues, I posted even more on the forums a few weeks ago. Unfortunately, the dev doesn't seem to be interested in responding. Which, considering the game has only been out a couple of months, is a bit disappointing.\n\nSo yeah, I do not recommend spending money on this game unless the devs make some serious improvements. Not likely, but if it happened, this could be a fun game.\n\nEDIT: Dev has noticed my feedback and says they're going to work on some of the issues I've raised, so that's something.",
